                "start_index": 308,
                "end_index": 461,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "What Mutual Funds Charge (The % Fee on Assets)\nWhen you invest in a mutual fund, you pay an annual fee known as the **expense ratio** (or management fee)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 463,
                "end_index": 530,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This fee is a percentage of the total Assets Under Management (AUM)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 532,
                "end_index": 618,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Actively Managed Funds:** Usually charge between **0.5% and 1.5%** of AUM annually"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 733,
                "end_index": 902,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "**Crucial Note:** Unlike hedge funds, mutual fund companies **do not** take a percentage of the profits (such as the famous \"20% performance fee\" charged by hedge funds)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 904,
                "end_index": 1037,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "By law, mutual funds must charge a flat percentage fee based on total assets, regardless of whether the fund goes up or down in value"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1172,
                "end_index": 1283,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Instead, they are salaried employees of an Asset Management Company (AMC) like Fidelity, Vanguard, or BlackRock"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1287,
                "end_index": 1417,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "According to financial industry studies, over **95% of mutual fund managers** are compensated using a **Salary + Bonus** structure"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1420,
                "end_index": 1591,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "#### **The Base Salary**\n* Typical base salaries for mutual fund managers range from **$200,000 to $450,000+** depending on seniority and the size of the fund they oversee"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1594,
                "end_index": 1736,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "#### **The Performance Bonus (The Real Money)**\nAbout **75% to 80%** of a manager\u2019s total compensation comes from performance-linked bonuses"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1738,
                "end_index": 1988,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "These bonuses are not a direct percentage of profits, but are calculated using specific formulas:\n* **Beating the Benchmark:** Managers are evaluated on whether they beat a specific benchmark (like the S&P 500) over a rolling 1-, 3-, or 5-year period"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2033,
                "end_index": 2182,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **AUM Growth:** Because AMCs make money on total asset size, managers are often rewarded for keeping clients happy and growing the size of the fund"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2186,
                "end_index": 2292,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Depending on performance, a manager's bonus can easily represent **50% to over 200% of their base salary**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2296,
                "end_index": 2495,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Average/Median Managers:** A Wharton study of U.S. mutual fund managers found that the median fund manager makes roughly **$462,000** in total compensation ($300,000 base salary + $162,000 bonus)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2497,
                "end_index": 2679,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Star Managers (95th Percentile):** Elite managers running multi-billion-dollar funds can earn upwards of **$4.9 million** per year ($1.6 million base salary + $3.3 million bonus)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10,
